1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:09,385
In the 8th century, an Indian Queen made an impossible vow: she would starve herself to death until she saw the pinnacle of a grand Shiva temple.

2
00:00:09,335 --> 00:00:11,679
Her engineers panicked.

3
00:00:11,679 --> 00:00:16,901
Building a 100-foot stone temple from the ground up would take twenty years!

4
00:00:16,901 --> 00:00:19,713
The Queen had only days to live.

5
00:00:19,713 --> 00:00:30,768
That's when master architect Kokasa stepped forward with an audacious idea: Instead of building from the ground up, he climbed to the top of the mountain and carved the temple from the top down!

6
00:00:30,768 --> 00:00:39,231
By day seven, the gleaming white spire was finished atop the peak, allowing the Queen to see the temple crown and break her fast!

7
00:00:39,231 --> 00:00:44,244
Meanwhile, ninety feet of mountain underneath was still untouched rock!

8
00:00:44,244 --> 00:00:51,302
Watch Episode Three of our full documentary linked below to see how ancient India pulled off the impossible!

